$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
$h = 'D:\GITHUB  Project\sangam-handoff'
$ts = [DateTime]::UtcNow.ToString('yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ssZ')
$enc = New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false)
function Board($kind, $text, $to) {
  if ($text.Contains('|') -or $to.Contains('|')) { throw "pipe in text: $text" }
  [IO.File]::AppendAllText("$h\WAVE4-SYNC-BOARD.md", "$ts | W4-I/B69 | $kind | $text | $to`n", $enc)
}

Board 'REQUEST' ('W4-G generator (decision 154, one separate SCIM table): new changeset after the SEC_* group, comment "SCIM provisioning state (M-099, decision 154)", table SEC_SCIM_RESOURCE columns tenant_id {str64} NOT NULL ; resource_type {vc16} NOT NULL (USER or GROUP) ; resource_id {str} NOT NULL (SEC_PERSON.person_id or SEC_GROUP.group_id) ; user_name {str} null (User userName as sent) ; name_key {str} NOT NULL (User: lower-case userName; Group: id:<resource_id>) ; external_id {str} null ; ' +
  'external_key {str} NOT NULL (x:<externalId> when set, otherwise id:<resource_id>; the service caps externalId at 253 chars) ; attributes {text} null (JSON of the SCIM core attributes Sangam keeps verbatim: name, emails, phoneNumbers, locale, preferredLanguage, timezone, title) ; version {long} NOT NULL (ETag counter) ; created_at {ts} NOT NULL ; updated_at {ts} NOT NULL. Primary key (tenant_id, resource_type, resource_id). Unique indexes SEC_SCIM_NAME (tenant_id, resource_type, name_key) and SEC_SCIM_EXT (tenant_id, resource_type, external_key). ' +
  'The two key columns are NOT NULL on purpose: SQL Server allows one NULL per unique index, so nullable userName or externalId cannot carry the RFC 7644 409 uniqueness on all five dialects. Please add it to SangamSchema PRODUCT_TABLES and to the security reference DDL if that is generated too, and tell me the changeset id.') 'W4-G'

Board 'REQUEST' ('W4-M contract routes/scim.py (decision 154: postings read-only, SCIM manages persons, groups and memberships only): (1) ScimSangamUser: personId, orgUnitId and postings readOnly true; postings description: Seats held (IX.5), read-only; a request that changes them gets 400 scimType mutability (an unchanged echo of the current list is accepted); (2) scimCreateUser description: Creates the person (USER_PROVISIONED); 409 uniqueness on userName or externalId; 400 mutability when postings are sent; ' +
  '(3) scimReplaceUser: active=false disables the person (USER_DISABLED) and revokes its API tokens; postings are not touched; (4) scimDeleteUser: Deactivates the person (history kept, X.2.3) and removes its SCIM group memberships; postings are not touched; 204; (5) header comment lines 8-11: drop SEAT_HOLDER_CHANGED from the SCIM audit list and replace the sentence on posting changes by: postings and seats are read-only in SCIM (decision 154); (6) ScimError description adds 400 mutability. ' +
  '(7) Groups: members of type Group give 400 invalidValue (no nested groups; SEC_GROUP_MEMBER holds persons only). (8) ServiceProviderConfig text unchanged. Please post DONE with the route file hash.') 'W4-M'

Board 'REQUEST' ('W4-B (decision 154, assignment 154 support): please grant W4-I new files only in sangam-security: package org.sangam.security.scim (ScimService, ScimFilter, ScimPatch, ScimResources, ScimException and their H2 unit tests, plus Oracle and SQL Server variants written and marked NOT_RUN). The service runs in the caller transaction with SecurityIdentity like LdapDirectorySync, requires USER ADMIN through AuthorizationService, writes SEC_PERSON, SEC_GROUP and SEC_GROUP_MEMBER with source SCIM through PersonService and GroupAdminService where those methods exist, re-enables a person by UPDATE status ACTIVE with USER_UPDATED how ENABLE (PersonService has no enable method), revokes API tokens on disable through ApiTokenService.revokeAllOf, ' +
  'and never touches SEC_POSTING or SEC_SEAT. Questions for you: (a) the IdP principal permission scim.provision, map it in SecurityPermissionBridge to USER ADMIN, or add a dedicated Permission; I propose USER ADMIN; (b) the OIDC subject of a SCIM user comes from externalId by default, userName by configuration, mirroring LdapDirectorySync userIdAttribute; an existing person with the same subject is adopted, not duplicated. If you prefer to code the security side yourself, say so and I send the exact method list.') 'W4-B'

Board 'REQUEST' 'integrator (decision 154): grant W4-I two NEW files in sangam-server: src/main/java/org/sangam/server/web/ScimController.java (thin Spring adapter for /scim/v2 over sangam-security ScimService, application/scim+json, SCIM error bodies) and src/main/java/org/sangam/server/config/ScimWiring.java (ScimService bean from the existing security beans), plus their tests under src/test/java/org/sangam/server/web. No existing server file changes. This keeps the SCIM protocol in sangam-security (framework independent, decision 137(4)) and avoids a new sangam-rest port and bridge.' 'integrator'

